  "user_impact": "Screen reader users hear a tab stop without a role and cannot tell what it is or how to operate it.",
  "technical_impact": "An element that is not natively focusable has a tabindex of 0 or more and no interactive role (generic, group, article, section, paragraph, none, presentation or no role at all), so Tab reaches it but a screen reader announces it without a role or an operable state; reported as a review hint, because a script may still make it operable.",
  "checks": [
